// `m.get(k)` gives `opt<V>`: some value when the key is present, none when
// it is absent. `?? fallback` takes the value or the fallback. `Map.get` is
// an engine op whose engine answers none with its null; PilIR and the
// emitted C used to read that answer as the opt record and stop at the
// first `??` ("cannot read `1` from integer"; found 2026-11-16 while
// probing for the PROP-021 lexer builder). The lowering now notes the
// answer as raw and tests it as nullable (selfhost/ir/lower_try.pilot
// `engine_call`, stand-in `ir.absent_as_null`).
//
// Expected, worked by hand:
//   "a" is present with 4         -> 4
//   "b" is absent, fallback 7     -> 7
//   3 is present in the i64 map   -> 4
fn main() {
    var m: Map<str, i64> = Map<str, i64>();
    m.set("a", 4);
    print(m.get("a") ?? 0);
    print(m.get("b") ?? 7);
    var n: Map<i64, i64> = Map<i64, i64>();
    n.set(3, 4);
    print(n.get(3) ?? 0);
}
